      "normalized_sha256": "cfb2314df4ea697cded9cf0262c9f9148799f41b14471c7e9e6718139a0df7cb",
      "rationale": "This guarded base equation defines trialChoice to return the carried result when the divisor scan has reached or passed N on its stated I >= 2 domain; it neither rewrites program execution nor asserts an independent mathematical fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-cfb2314df4ea697cded9cf0262c9f9148799f41b14471c7e9e6718139a0df7cb",
      "start_line": 17,
      "text": "  rule trialChoice(N, I, R, _Y) => R\n    requires I >=Int N andBool I >=Int 2"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 22,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "7877c000c080d739794dbb3915705fc950212640a5d2b537a5a03a482090b6b0",
      "rationale": "This is the divisor branch of the guarded trialChoice recurrence, defining the next summary term after a zero remainder by carrying Y forward; it is an equation for the named summary rather than an operational or separately proved rule.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-7877c000c080d739794dbb3915705fc950212640a5d2b537a5a03a482090b6b0",
      "start_line": 20,
      "text": "  rule trialChoice(N, I, _R, Y) => trialChoice(N, I +Int 1, Y, Y)\n    requires I >=Int 2 andBool I <Int N\n      andBool pyMod(N, I) ==Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 26,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "8c56ab5c7a8fcd164fb0d555a596cba2218ac3044885d21f8baf67a9b169c995",
      "rationale": "This is the non-divisor branch of the guarded trialChoice recurrence, defining the next summary term after a nonzero remainder by preserving R; it defines the summary and does not add a reusable domain fact.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-8c56ab5c7a8fcd164fb0d555a596cba2218ac3044885d21f8baf67a9b169c995",
      "start_line": 24,
      "text": "  rule trialChoice(N, I, R, Y) => trialChoice(N, I +Int 1, R, Y)\n    requires I >=Int 2 andBool I <Int N\n      andBool pyMod(N, I) =/=Int 0"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 29,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "a0b42dd3540472c0a1673da37721faef739d8c78131d66bce39a209f91709162",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the N < 2 case of the total xOrYSpec summary to select Y; it is one disjoint case of a named proof-term definition.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-a0b42dd3540472c0a1673da37721faef739d8c78131d66bce39a209f91709162",
      "start_line": 28,
      "text": "  rule xOrYSpec(N, _X, Y) => Y\n    requires N <Int 2"
    },
    {
      "attributes": [],
      "classification": "DEFINITION",
      "end_line": 32,
      "module": "VERIFICATION",
      "normalized_sha256": "9fda901ff7675dee4a02c075bdb95e6d8c069630f55a40d4ecadca1361519e44",
      "rationale": "This guarded equation defines the N >= 2 case of xOrYSpec by delegating to trialChoice from candidate 2; it completes the named summary definition and is not established separately before being imported.",
      "source_rule_id": "rule-9fda901ff7675dee4a02c075bdb95e6d8c069630f55a40d4ecadca1361519e44",
      "start_line": 31,
      "text": "  rule xOrYSpec(N, X, Y) => trialChoice(N, 2, X, Y)\n    requires N >=Int 2"
    }
  ],
